&lt;p&gt;Reduce Unwanted Subscriptions&lt;br&gt;
Newsletters and promotional emails can gradually fill an old Yahoo inbox.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Over time, users may subscribe to websites that they no longer use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unsubscribing from unnecessary mailing lists can reduce clutter and make important emails easier to identify.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should be cautious when interacting with unfamiliar unsubscribe links. When a message appears suspicious, it may be safer to manage subscriptions directly through the relevant legitimate service.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Protect Against Phishing Emails&lt;br&gt;
Phishing is an important concern for every email user.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A phishing message may attempt to convince someone that an urgent action is required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, a fraudulent email may claim that:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The account will be closed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A payment failed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A security issue was detected&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A password must be confirmed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A package is waiting&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A verification process is required&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users should carefully inspect unexpected messages before clicking links or entering information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Important warning signs include unusual sender addresses, unexpected attachments, urgent language, suspicious links, and requests for passwords or verification codes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do Not Share Passwords or Verification Codes&lt;br&gt;
Passwords and verification codes should remain private.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Legitimate services generally have specific procedures for account security and recovery. Users should be cautious if someone contacts them unexpectedly and asks for login credentials or verification information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A verification code should never be shared simply because another person claims to need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keeping these details private is one of the simplest ways to reduce account-security risks.&lt;/p&gt;

