&lt;p&gt;Myth 4: Password protection is the only security requirement&lt;br&gt;
Strong passwords are important, but recovery settings, device management, security reviews, and phishing awareness also matter.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Myth 5: Every old email should be saved&lt;br&gt;
Only information that remains useful or necessary needs to be retained. Unnecessary messages can be removed according to the user's needs.&lt;/p&gt;

