&lt;h3&gt;


💬 Let's Discuss
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How does your team currently manage in-app announcements and feature onboarding? Do you hardcode modals into React, use an external script, or automate via MCP? Drop your thoughts below!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(If you're building with Next.js or AI coding agents, check out &lt;a href="https://www.neotic.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Neotic&lt;/a&gt; and our remote MCP endpoint at &lt;code&gt;https://www.neotic.app/api/mcp&lt;/code&gt;!)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


TypeScript 6.0 &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt;: What Changes When Iterators Finally Have Correct Return Types
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This article was written with the assistance of AI, under human supervision and review.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most iterator type safety problems stem from a single design decision made in TypeScript 2.3: the return value of &lt;code&gt;iterator.next()&lt;/code&gt; was typed as &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; for built-in iterators. This worked well enough for basic iteration, but it allowed dangerous type mismatches to slip through whenever code called &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;.throw()&lt;/code&gt; on an iterator. TypeScript 6.0 closes this loophole with &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt;, and the changes will surface bugs in code that assumed iterator protocol methods could accept arbitrary values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The problem manifests when developers pass values to iterator methods that the iterator cannot actually handle. Array iterators, for example, ignore the argument to &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; entirely, but TypeScript allowed any type to flow through unchecked. This silent mismatch meant runtime behavior and type signatures diverged in ways that only became visible during refactoring or when debugging unexpected iterator state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fc6mlqmh0mcawvvpsqlep.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fc6mlqmh0mcawvvpsqlep.png" width="796" height="108"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TypeScript 6.0 changes this by setting &lt;code&gt;BuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; when &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt; is enabled. This means built-in iterators now correctly reflect their actual behavior: they do not consume or propagate return values. The type system finally matches the JavaScript specification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fm9szug2vyiso0c20kdem.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fm9szug2vyiso0c20kdem.png" width="796" height="108"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Key Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built-in iterators in TypeScript now return &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; when calling &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;.throw()&lt;/code&gt; under &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code that passes values to iterator protocol methods will produce type errors, revealing previously silent bugs where those values were ignored at runtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The flag is not part of &lt;code&gt;--strict&lt;/code&gt; by default in TypeScript 6.0, giving teams time to migrate before a future major version enforces it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Migration requires auditing iterator-consuming code for manual &lt;code&gt;.next()&lt;/code&gt; calls with arguments, explicit &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; invocations, and generator functions that yield or return typed values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opt-out remains available for codebases that depend on legacy iterator libraries expecting the old &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Understanding BuiltinIteratorReturn and Why It Defaulted to &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;BuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt; type parameter controls what TypeScript infers as the return type when you call &lt;code&gt;.return(value)&lt;/code&gt; on a built-in iterator. Before TypeScript 6.0, this parameter defaulted to &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt;, which meant the compiler accepted any value passed to iterator protocol methods without validation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This design choice solved a practical problem in 2017: JavaScript iterators existed in the wild with inconsistent return value handling, and TypeScript needed to support them all without breaking existing code. The decision to use &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; made migration easier but introduced a type hole that developers exploited unknowingly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When you enable &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt;, TypeScript changes &lt;code&gt;BuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt; from &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt;. This reflects the actual behavior of built-in JavaScript iterators: array iterators, string iterators, and set iterators all ignore the argument passed to &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt;. The specification defines this as a no-op for these iterator types.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The consequence is immediate: code that passed typed values to &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; will now produce type errors. These errors are not false positives. They reveal places where your code assumed the iterator would consume a value, but the runtime ignored it. The type system was lying, and now it tells the truth.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fd51ztamsq8i0icmeq7dm.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fd51ztamsq8i0icmeq7dm.png" width="800" height="1194"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The type parameter matters most for generator functions and custom iterators that return meaningful values from &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt;. A generator that yields numbers but returns a string when closed has a return type that must match the iterator protocol. Under the old rules, TypeScript allowed mismatches. Under the new rules, the types must align exactly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt; Changes Iterator Type Inference
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The flag affects how TypeScript infers the &lt;code&gt;TReturn&lt;/code&gt; parameter in &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T, TReturn, TNext&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Built-in iterators like arrays, maps, and strings now infer &lt;code&gt;TReturn&lt;/code&gt; as &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt;, which cascades through every function that accepts or returns an iterator.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This change is visible in three places: explicit iterator method calls, for-of loops that interact with iterator state, and generator functions that yield values. The most common breaks occur in code that manually drives an iterator by calling &lt;code&gt;.next()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;.throw()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;consumeIterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// This line now produces a type error&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;cleanup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;numbers&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;][&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Symbol&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;consumeIterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;numbers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The error message is specific: &lt;code&gt;Argument of type '{ cleanup: boolean }' is not assignable to parameter of type 'undefined'&lt;/code&gt;. The iterator does not accept a cleanup object because built-in iterators do not process return values. The code was always wrong, but TypeScript 5.x accepted it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix depends on intent. If the goal was to signal cleanup to a custom iterator, the function signature must specify that the iterator accepts return values. If the goal was to close the iterator without passing data, remove the argument entirely.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Correct approach 1: Accept only iterators with return values&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;consumeIteratorWithCleanup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;cleanup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;cleanup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Correct approach 2: Close without passing data&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;consumeIterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The second approach works with built-in iterators because &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; is optional and can be called without arguments. The type system now enforces this distinction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Real-World Code That Breaks When You Enable This Flag
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The most common break appears in middleware that wraps iterators for logging, rate-limiting, or transformation. These wrappers often pass arbitrary metadata to &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; under the assumption that the underlying iterator might use it. Under &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt;, TypeScript rejects this unless the wrapper explicitly types the iterator to accept return values.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;RateLimitedIterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;implements&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;constructor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;IteratorResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;IteratorResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Type error: source.return expects undefined&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;span class="na"&gt;rateLimited&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;delay&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The wrapper assumes the source iterator will handle the metadata, but built-in iterators ignore it. The fix is to remove the argument or change the source type to a custom iterator that accepts return values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another common break occurs in generator functions that return typed values. Before TypeScript 6.0, a generator could return any type without matching the iterator return signature. Now the types must align exactly.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;generateWithMetadata&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Generator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;yield&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;yield&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Return value must be string, not number&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;42&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Type error&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This catches real bugs. If code expected the generator to return a string for cleanup or logging, but the generator returned a number, the mismatch would cause silent failures downstream. TypeScript now surfaces this at compile time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Comparing Iterator vs Iterator in Practice
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The difference between these two signatures is subtle but expensive when it matters. An iterator typed with &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; as the return parameter accepts any value passed to &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt;, while an iterator typed with &lt;code&gt;undefined&lt;/code&gt; rejects everything except undefined.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5j3yuz4pfs6ilkegn7vt.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F5j3yuz4pfs6ilkegn7vt.png" width="800" height="251"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The practical consequence appears in code that chains iterators or composes them with utility functions. A function that accepts &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T, any&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; allows callers to pass built-in iterators with false type safety. A function that accepts &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T, undefined&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; enforces correct usage at the call site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider a function that exhausts an iterator and returns collected values. Under the old rules, the function could accept any iterator and call &lt;code&gt;.return(metadata)&lt;/code&gt; without type errors, even though built-in iterators ignore metadata.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Old signature (dangerous)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;exhaust&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;exhausted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Silently ignored&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// New signature (safe)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;exhaust&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Type-safe&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The new signature prevents callers from passing values to &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt;, which matches runtime behavior. The old signature allowed it, which created a false impression that the iterator would process the value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This distinction is critical when migrating large codebases. Functions typed with &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T, any&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; must be audited manually because TypeScript cannot infer which iterators actually use return values and which ignore them. The compiler can only check syntax, not intent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Migration Strategy: Fixing Iterator-Based Code for TypeScript 6.0
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The migration path starts with enabling &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt; in a test environment and collecting type errors. These errors fall into three categories: explicit &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; calls with arguments, generator functions with mismatched return types, and utility functions that accept overly permissive iterator signatures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F6xcug7pvlgxzyggs1udd.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F6xcug7pvlgxzyggs1udd.png" width="798" height="133"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For each error, the first question is whether the return value was intentional. If the code called &lt;code&gt;.return(metadata)&lt;/code&gt; but the iterator is a built-in array or string iterator, the argument was always ignored. Remove it. If the code called &lt;code&gt;.return(value)&lt;/code&gt; on a custom iterator that actually processes the value, change the type signature to reflect that.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generator functions require special attention because their return type must match both the explicit return statement and the iterator protocol. A generator that yields numbers and returns a string must be typed as &lt;code&gt;Generator&amp;lt;number, string, void&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, not &lt;code&gt;Generator&amp;lt;number&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Before: implicit any return&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processItems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[])&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;yield&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;complete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Implicitly any&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// After: explicit return type&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processItems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Generator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;yield&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;complete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The third category involves utility functions that wrap or transform iterators. These functions must decide whether they accept only built-in iterators or support custom iterators with return values. The choice affects the type signature and determines which iterators can be passed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A transformer that only works with built-in iterators should use &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T, undefined&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. A transformer that supports custom iterators should use &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T, TReturn&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; and propagate the return type through the transformation.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Built-in iterators only&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Custom iterators with return values&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TReturn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TReturn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Iterator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TReturn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;TReturn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;iter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;??&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The second version preserves the return type, which allows custom iterators to propagate cleanup signals or final values through the transformation. The first version discards return values, which is correct for built-in iterators but breaks custom iterator semantics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When to Explicitly Opt Out of strictBuiltinIteratorReturn
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Opt-out is necessary when migrating a codebase that depends on third-party iterator libraries written before TypeScript 6.0. These libraries often typed iterator return values as &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; because that was the only way to support both built-in and custom iterators without excessive type annotations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The decision to opt out should be temporary. Long-term type safety depends on migrating these libraries or wrapping them with correct types. Disabling the flag indefinitely means accepting silent bugs in iterator protocol code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk2fpl0numex59fw2j9jo.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fk2fpl0numex59fw2j9jo.png" width="800" height="221"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A second reason to opt out is when the codebase uses iterator-heavy abstractions that would require weeks of refactoring to align with the new types. In this case, the team should plan a dedicated migration sprint rather than attempting to fix everything during a routine upgrade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The opt-out configuration is straightforward. Set &lt;code&gt;strictBuiltinIteratorReturn: false&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;tsconfig.json&lt;/code&gt; to disable the flag even when &lt;code&gt;--strict&lt;/code&gt; is enabled. This allows incremental migration without blocking other strict mode features.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;compilerOptions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;strict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Teams should track the opt-out as technical debt and prioritize migration before TypeScript 7.0, where the flag will likely become non-optional under &lt;code&gt;--strict&lt;/code&gt;. The type system is moving toward correctness, and delaying migration only increases the eventual cost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Frequently Asked Questions
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Does enabling strictBuiltinIteratorReturn break for-of loops?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. For-of loops do not call &lt;code&gt;.return()&lt;/code&gt; explicitly, so they remain type-safe regardless of the flag. The flag only affects code that manually drives iterators by calling protocol methods.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Can I enable this flag without enabling all of strict mode?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes. The flag is independent and can be enabled even when &lt;code&gt;strict&lt;/code&gt; is false. Set &lt;code&gt;"strictBuiltinIteratorReturn": true&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;tsconfig.json&lt;/code&gt; to opt in selectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Why did TypeScript wait until 6.0 to make this change?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The change required breaking existing code that relied on the &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt; behavior, which violates TypeScript's stability guarantees for minor versions. Major versions allow breaking changes, so TypeScript 6.0 was the first opportunity to fix this long-standing type hole.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What happens to generators that return void?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Generators that return void are unaffected. The flag only changes inference for iterators that explicitly return typed values. A generator with no return statement or a return statement without a value continues to work as before.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Do I need to update third-party iterator libraries?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only if those libraries expose iterator return types in their public API. Libraries that return opaque iterators or use &lt;code&gt;Iterator&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; without specifying return types will continue to work without changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion: Why This Flag Matters for Long-Term Type Safety
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn&lt;/code&gt; flag closes a type safety gap that existed since TypeScript 2.3. Built-in iterators now have correct return types that match their runtime behavior, which prevents silent bugs where code passed values to iterator methods that ignored them. The migration cost is real, but the payoff is a type system that tells the truth about iterator protocol semantics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Teams should enable the flag during the next major upgrade cycle and plan time to fix type errors systematically. The errors reveal places where types and runtime behavior diverged, which means fixing them improves code quality beyond satisfying the compiler. That covers the essential patterns for TypeScript 6.0 iterator types. Apply these in production and the difference will be immediate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For broader context on migrating to TypeScript 6.0, see &lt;a href="https://jsmanifest.com/typescript-5-to-6-migration-200k-lines" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 5 to 6 Migration: 200K Lines&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jsmanifest.com/typescript-6-migration-guide" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript 6 Migration Guide&lt;/a&gt;. If you work with form validation where iterator types surface in field processing, &lt;a href="https://jsmanifest.com/typescript-form-validators-custom" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TypeScript Form Validators Custom&lt;/a&gt; covers the practical implications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A user searches for “react”, then quickly changes the search to “react hooks”. The second request finishes first. A moment later, results for the older search replace the current results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The network did not necessarily fail. The UI accepted a response that no longer belonged to the current request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is a useful interview exercise because it tests reasoning about time, state and cleanup—not just whether you remember a Hook name.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Draw the sequence first
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Time&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Event&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Request A starts for “react”&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Request B starts for “react hooks”&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;B finishes; the UI shows B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A finishes; an unguarded callback overwrites B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The requirement is not “use the last response to arrive.” It is “only the request belonging to the current search may update this result state.”&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clarify the intended loading experience as well. Should old results remain visible with a loading indicator, or disappear immediately? That is separate from preventing an obsolete response from winning.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Describe ownership, then implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each search operation needs a way to determine whether it is still current when its asynchronous work finishes. In an Effect-based implementation, cleanup can mark an old operation inactive. React's &lt;a href="https://react.dev/learn/synchronizing-with-effects#fetching-data" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Effect documentation&lt;/a&gt; describes aborting a fetch or ignoring its obsolete result during cleanup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The following small JavaScript model demonstrates result ownership. It is not a complete React component or a production fetching library:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createLatestResultGate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;let&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;generation&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;begin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mine&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;++&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;generation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mine&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;generation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;invalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;generation&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;gate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createLatestResultGate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isCurrentA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;gate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;begin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isCurrentB&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;gate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;begin&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isCurrentB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;B owns the current result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isCurrentA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;A must not update the result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;gate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;invalidate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;isCurrentB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Cleanup invalidates B too&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This models the ordering rule without needing unpredictable network delays. A real integration must keep the gate scoped to the appropriate component/request lifecycle; recreating it for every callback would defeat the comparison. An Effect-local inactive flag is often simpler for one Effect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Guard more than successful data
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An obsolete request can also clear a loading indicator or display an error after a newer request succeeds. Apply the ownership rule to every asynchronous state transition associated with the request, including error handling and finalization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, if A fails after B succeeds, the user should not suddenly see A's error presented as the status of B. That case belongs in the test plan alongside out-of-order successes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Debouncing answers a different question
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Delaying a request until typing pauses may reduce how many operations start. It does not establish which already-started request owns the current state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In an interview, separate the two requirements explicitly: controlling request frequency and preventing stale updates. Choosing one does not demonstrate that the other is solved.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Test sequences, not just the happy path
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use controllable promises or a request mock so the test decides completion order:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A starts, B starts, B succeeds, then A succeeds: B must remain visible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A starts, B starts, B succeeds, then A fails: A's error must not replace B's status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A starts, then the component unmounts: the old operation must not update its state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The latest request fails: the current error must still be shown.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also explain what happens to loading state in each sequence. Merely hiding every error would make one test pass while breaking the actual feature.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Avoid rebuilding your entire data layer in the interview
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the application already uses a framework loader or client-side query cache, explain how its request identity, cancellation and cache behavior apply. React discusses the limitations of manual fetching in Effects in its &lt;a href="https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect#fetching-data-with-effects" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;useEffect reference&lt;/a&gt;. A small example proves understanding; it does not justify replacing the application's existing data layer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Disclosure: I am Raviindra Wadile, creator of &lt;a href="https://wasasked.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;wasAsked&lt;/a&gt;. I use interview questions as prompts for explaining behavior and testing assumptions. The site offers public question browsing and a browser-local practice shortlist; this article is an educational exercise, not a report of a production incident.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cuando se habla de rendimiento frontend, casi siempre aparecen los mismos números: tiempo de carga, tamaño del bundle y Core Web Vitals. Son útiles, pero no cuentan toda la historia. Una pantalla puede pintar rápido y seguir siendo dificil de usar si el botón no anuncia que está ocupado, si el foco salta al validar o si una animación tapa el mensaje de error.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;En proyectos de React he encontrado que una mejora de rendimiento sostenible tiene dos resultados: la interfaz responde antes y la persona entiende mejor qué está pasando. Ese segundo resultado suele perderse en los dashboards. Incluso cuando alguien busca un temp mail for facebook para probar un flujo, el formulario sigue necesitando estados claros, teclado y mensajes comprensibles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


El rendimiento no termina en los milisegundos
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un formulario de registro puede tener una respuesta rápida y aun así sentirse lento. Por ejemplo, el usuario pulsa “Continuar”, no cambia nada visual, y vuelve a pulsar. La API recibe dos solicitudes y la interfaz parece rota. La solución no es solo bajar unos milisegundos: es hacer visible el estado de la acción.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Antes de optimizar, separo tres medidas:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Rendimiento técnico:&lt;/strong&gt; cuánto tarda en pintar y responder.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Rendimiento percibido:&lt;/strong&gt; cuánto tarda la persona en saber si su acción funcionó.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Rendimiento inclusivo:&lt;/strong&gt; si esa información llega también con teclado, lector de pantalla o movimiento reducido.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esta separación cambia las prioridades. Un spinner bonito no corrige un botón sin nombre accesible; un memo innecesario tampoco arregla una validación que borra el mensaje anterior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Un patrón de React para estados que explican lo que pasa
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Un componente pequeño puede modelar el flujo con estados explícitos. No hace falta introducir una librería para cada formulario:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;SubmitButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;busy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"submit"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;disabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;busy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-busy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;busy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;busy&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Guardando…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Guardar cambios&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;El atributo &lt;code&gt;disabled&lt;/code&gt; evita dobles envíos, mientras que &lt;code&gt;aria-busy&lt;/code&gt; comunica el estado a tecnologías de asistencia. Después del envío, el resultado debería vivir en una región estable:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"polite"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Cambios guardados.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;No se pudo guardar. Revisa los campos e inténtalo otra vez.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;El detalle importante es que el nodo no aparece y desaparece sin necesidad. Si su posición cambia en cada render, el lector de pantalla y el usuario de teclado tienen más trabajo. También conviene mantener la respuesta del servidor cerca del campo correspondiente, no solo en un toast que desaparece.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para probar flujos que dependen de correo, ayuda separar la interfaz de la infraestructura. Las &lt;a href="https://dev.to/silviutech/fastapi-pruebas-de-signup-sin-inbox-real-4jg9"&gt;pruebas de signup sin inbox real&lt;/a&gt; muestran una dirección útil para aislar el backend. Y una &lt;a href="https://dev.to/silviutech/fastapi-cola-visible-para-correos-async-419m"&gt;cola visible para correos async&lt;/a&gt; recuerda que también debemos poder explicar cuándo llegó una señal externa.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


CSS y accesibilidad: menos movimiento, más control
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Los cambios de layout son una fuente silenciosa de frustración. Reservar espacio para mensajes de error y usar un contenedor con altura razonable reduce saltos visuales. Para las animaciones, la preferencia del sistema merece una regla sencilla:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@media&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;prefers-reduced-motion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;reduce&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;*,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;::before&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nd"&gt;::after&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;animation-duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0.01ms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;animation-iteration-count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nl"&gt;transition-duration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;0.01ms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;scroll-behavior&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;auto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No conviene quitar todos los cambios de estado. Una frontera, un texto o un cambio de color con suficiente contraste puede comunicar progreso sin marear. Reviso el foco con Tab, aumento el zoom al 200% y compruebo que el mensaje no dependa solamente del color. A veces el contraste queda un poco raro en el primer intento, asi que lo mido y no me fio solo del ojo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Cómo medir si el cambio ayudó
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mido la interacción completa, no solo el render. Algunas señales prácticas son el tiempo hasta que el botón comunica el resultado, la cantidad de envíos duplicados y el número de usuarios que corrigen el mismo campo más de una vez. Para una vista concreta, una métrica simple puede ser:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;tiempo_de_confirmacion = resultado_visible - click_inicial
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Luego comparo antes y después con el mismo escenario de red y dispositivo. No inventaría una mejora a partir de una sola sesión. Un pequeño log con estado, duración y motivo de error suele ser más útil que diez capturas de pantalla.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Checklist para revisar un formulario
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿El botón cambia de estado inmediatamente?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿Se bloquean los envíos duplicados sin bloquear la navegación?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿El foco llega al primer error real?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿Cada error tiene texto, no solo color o icono?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿La respuesta vive en una región anunciable?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿La interfaz funciona con movimiento reducido y zoom alto?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;¿Puedes relacionar una queja con un estado y una duración concretos?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La accesibilidad no es una capa que se añade después de optimizar. Es parte de la respuesta del producto. Cuando React, CSS y los eventos externos comparten estados claros, la interfaz se siente más rápida porque requiere menos adivinanzas. Ese es un tipo de rendimiento que los usuarios notan, aunque no siempre aparezca en Lighthouse.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;


Cómo solucionar "Text content does not match server-rendered HTML" en Next.js App Router
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Este error ocurre cuando el HTML generado en el servidor (&lt;code&gt;server-side rendering&lt;/code&gt;) no coincide con el árbol de React generado durante la primera renderización en el navegador (&lt;code&gt;client-side hydration&lt;/code&gt;). React detecta esta inconsistencia y lanza una advertencia crítica porque puede romper la interactividad y causar comportamientos impredecibles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Causa raíz
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;La mayoría de los casos se deben a:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uso de APIs del navegador (&lt;code&gt;window&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Date.now()&lt;/code&gt;, etc.) &lt;strong&gt;directamente en el renderizado&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lógica condicional basada en &lt;code&gt;typeof window !== 'undefined'&lt;/code&gt; dentro del cuerpo del componente (no dentro de &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elementos HTML anidados inválidos según el estándar (ej. &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; dentro de otro &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; dentro de &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensiones del navegador que modifican el DOM antes de la hidratación.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metaetiqueta de detección automática de iOS (&lt;code&gt;format-detection&lt;/code&gt;) que inyecta &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; dinámicos en números de teléfono o fechas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Solución definitiva (pasos verificados)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Paso 1: Aisla la fuente de la inconsistencia
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Busca en tu código:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uso directo de &lt;code&gt;window&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;navigator&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Date()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt;, etc. en el cuerpo del componente.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lógica condicional como &lt;code&gt;if (typeof window !== 'undefined') { ... }&lt;/code&gt; fuera de hooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ejemplo problemático:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ INCORRECTO: Se ejecuta en SSR y en CSR con resultados distintos&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Timestamp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ Diferente en SSR vs CSR&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLocaleString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Paso 2: Aplica la solución según el caso
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


🔹 Caso A: Contenido dinámico (fechas, IDs aleatorios, etc.)
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Usa &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; en el elemento problemático:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ CORRECTO: Advertencia suprimida solo en el elemento afectado&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLocaleString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ &lt;strong&gt;Importante&lt;/strong&gt;: Solo aplica a elementos &lt;em&gt;textuales&lt;/em&gt; y de un solo nivel de profundidad.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;


🔹 Caso B: Lógica que requiere el navegador (ej. &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;window.innerWidth&lt;/code&gt;)
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Usa &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; para postergar la lógica al cliente:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ CORRECTO: Renderiza lo mismo en SSR y CSR inicialmente&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ThemeToggle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Valor por defecto seguro&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;localStorage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;stored&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Toggle&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h4&gt;


🔹 Caso C: Componente totalmente client-side (ej. canvas, mapas)
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desactiva SSR con &lt;code&gt;dynamic&lt;/code&gt; y &lt;code&gt;ssr: false&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// pages/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;dynamic&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;next/dynamic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;InteractiveMap&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;dynamic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;../components/Map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; 
&lt;span class="na"&gt;ssr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;loading&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Cargando mapa...&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;InteractiveMap&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Paso 3: Verifica estructura HTML válida
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Revisa que no haya:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; anidados (ej. &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;...&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; → inválido).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; dentro de &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, o viceversa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ul&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ol&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; dentro de &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; dentro de &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ejemplo corregido:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ INCORRECTO&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/home"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Home&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; | &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/about"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;About&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ CORRECTO (usar &amp;lt;span&amp;gt; o fragmento)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/home"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Home&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; | &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;href&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"/about"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;About&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


✅ Paso 4: Deshabilita detección automática en iOS (si aplica)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Agrega esta metaetiqueta en &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;head&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; de tu layout:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/layout.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;RootLayout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ReactNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"es"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"format-detection"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"telephone=no, date=no, email=no, address=no"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;head&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;children&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


Pro-tip: Diagnóstico rápido
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Activa React DevTools&lt;/strong&gt; → Selecciona la pestaña "Components" y busca el ícono de advertencia (⚠️) en el árbol.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Busca en consola&lt;/strong&gt;: El error muestra la ruta exacta del componente afectado (ej. &lt;code&gt;at div (app/page.tsx:15:10)&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Prueba en modo incógnito&lt;/strong&gt;: Si desaparece el error, es una extensión del navegador (común: Grammarly, Dark Reader, ad blockers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Código corregido (ejemplo completo)
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ClientOnlyContent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Cargando...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ✅ Solo se ejecuta en cliente&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Contenido generado en el cliente&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;clearTimeout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;timer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;App Router&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ClientOnlyContent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* ✅ Supresión segura para fechas dinámicas */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Última actualización: &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLocaleDateString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



